{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_4b906f33e7e0544555015db59abaf331ebcee4f54be2bad1ed3002946a9590d8", "title": "Sword Art Online", "text": "Sword Art Online (Japanese: ソードアート・オンライン , Hepburn: Sōdo Āto Onrain ) is a Japanese light novel series written by Reki Kawahara and illustrated by abec. The series takes place in the near future and focuses on various virtual reality MMORPG worlds.", "score": 31.1328}, {"id": "hp_doc_2cf2b72965e8e9bc76a5ef2c76445866efdba93491369383dd9aa6f05a54e57a", "title": "Bryce Papenbrook", "text": "Bryce Papenbrook (born February 24, 1986) is an American voice actor. He has done voice work for Animaze, Bang Zoom! Entertainment, Funimation, and Studiopolis and has performed the voices for several anime roles, particularly those of young male protagonists. He is best known for his portrayals of Rin Okumura in \"Blue Exorcist\", Kirito in \"Sword Art Online\", Masaomi Kida in \"Durarara!! \" series, Eren Jaeger in \"Attack on Titan\", Caesar Anthonio Zeppeli in \"JoJo's Bizarre Adventure\", Shirou Emiya in \"\", Meliodas in \"The Seven Deadly Sins\", Red in \"Pokémon Origins\", Kaito in \"\", and Makoto Naegi and Nagito Komaeda in the \"Danganronpa\" series. In animation, he provides the voice of Adrien Agreste a.k.a. Cat Noir in \"\".", "score": 20.5347}, {"id": "hp_doc_bf8f079dbe4a5a61c209226ffea45f7ef3ca73dc946ea4e5472350ec2653c464", "title": "Kono Light Novel ga Sugoi!", "text": "Kono Light Novel ga Sugoi! (このライトノベルがすごい! , Kono Raito Noberu ga Sugoi! , lit. \"This Light Novel is Amazing!\") is an annual light novel guide book published by Takarajimasha. The guide book publishes a list of the top ten most popular light novels and their characters according to readers polled on the Internet. An introduction to each of the works comes with each listing, along with an interview of the light novel's author or authors for first place. Many of the light novels that have been listed in this guide book were later adapted into anime series. Most of the light novels listed contain a series of volumes, but some single-volume light novels also get listed. The first release of the guide book was on November 26, 2004 and is the 2005 listing. The latest release is the thirteenth volume on November 24, 2016 and is the 2017 listing. \" Toaru Majutsu no Index\" has appeared in the top ten in nine out of thirteen issues of \"Kono Light Novel ga Sugoi!\" , while \"Sword Art Online\" has appeared in seven, \"Baka to Test to Shōkanjū\" has appeared in six, and the \"Haruhi Suzumiya\" series and the \"Book Girl\" series have appeared in five.", "score": 15.6216}], "remaining_searches": 1}
